{"paper": "SSC-GD-17-Feb-2025-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 20, "tagged_count": 20, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "What time (in seconds) is required for a 238 m long train to cross a 702 m long tunnel, if the train travels at a speed of 36 km/h?", "options": [{"text": "94", "added": false}, {"text": "90", "added": false}, {"text": "100", "added": false}, {"text": "104", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "train-vs-platform", "key_answer": "94"}, {"n": 2, "text": "How many kilograms of sugar at ₹3.80 per kg should be mixed with 60 kgs of sugar at ₹4.60 per kg, so that by selling the mixture at ₹5 per kg, there may be gain of 25%?", "options": [{"text": "160 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "180 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "170 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "190 kg", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mixture-Alligation", "sub": "mixture-price", "key_answer": "180 kg"}, {"n": 3, "text": "To do a certain work, Q and R work on alternate days, with Q beginning the work on the first day. Q can finish the work alone in 56 days. If the work gets completed in 37.5 days, then R alone can finish half of the same work in:", "options": [{"text": "28 days", "added": false}, {"text": "21 days", "added": false}, {"text": "14 days", "added": false}, {"text": "7 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "alternate-days", "key_answer": "14 days"}, {"n": 4, "text": "The third proportional to 0.13 and 0.52 is:", "options": [{"text": "1.45", "added": false}, {"text": "3.12", "added": false}, {"text": "2.65", "added": false}, {"text": "2.08", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": "2.08"}, {"n": 5, "text": "Evaluate: (-9) - (-60) ÷ (-12) + (-3) × 8", "options": [{"text": "-38", "added": false}, {"text": "-37", "added": false}, {"text": "-41", "added": false}, {"text": "-40", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "-38"}, {"n": 6, "text": "The simple interest on a principal amount (in ₹) is ₹486 for a period of 3 years at the rate of 8% per annum. The principal amount (in ₹) is:", "options": [{"text": "2015", "added": false}, {"text": "2027", "added": false}, {"text": "2029", "added": false}, {"text": "2025", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "rate-time-principal", "key_answer": "2025"}, {"n": 7, "text": "The LCM of 18, 72, 184 and 144 is:", "options": [{"text": "3388", "added": false}, {"text": "3351", "added": false}, {"text": "3312", "added": false}, {"text": "3220", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": "3312"}, {"n": 8, "text": "The population of a district is 340000, out of which 217000 are males. 11% of the population is literate. If 11% males are literate, then what percentage of females are literate?", "options": [{"text": "12%", "added": false}, {"text": "14%", "added": false}, {"text": "13%", "added": false}, {"text": "11%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": "11%"}, {"n": 9, "text": "Evaluate: 16 + 10 ÷ 5 - 3 × 3", "options": [{"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "9"}, {"n": 10, "text": "The average weight of Chetan, Vipul and Mohan is 46 kg. If the average weight of Chetan and Vipul be 40 kg and that of Vipul and Mohan be 44 kg, then the weight of Vipul (in kg) is:", "options": [{"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}, {"text": "45", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "30"}, {"n": 11, "text": "When difference between compound and simple interest for three years is ₹122 at 5% interest per annum, the principal is ₹______", "options": [{"text": "16000", "added": false}, {"text": "15425", "added": false}, {"text": "16420", "added": false}, {"text": "17200", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "si-ci-difference", "key_answer": "16000"}, {"n": 12, "text": "The ice compartment in a refrigerator is 36 cm deep, 16 cm high and 12 cm wide. How many ice cubes will it hold, if each cube is 4 cm as its edge?", "options": [{"text": "216", "added": false}, {"text": "54", "added": false}, {"text": "108", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": "108"}, {"n": 13, "text": "Find the value of", "options": [{"text": "347", "added": false}, {"text": "336", "added": false}, {"text": "349", "added": false}, {"text": "325", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "336"}, {"n": 14, "text": "There are three persons M,N And P. They are running in the same direction around a circular track of length 150 m. Their speeds are 20 m/sec,15 m/sec and 12 m/sec, respectively. If they start at same time and same point, then after what time do they meet for the first time?", "options": [{"text": "165", "added": true}, {"text": "150", "added": false}, {"text": "151", "added": true}, {"text": "135", "added": true}], "options_source": "added", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "circular-track", "key_answer": "150 sec"}, {"n": 15, "text": "Mohan sold 153 chairs and had a gain equal to the selling price of 68 chairs. What is his profit percentage?", "options": [{"text": "80%", "added": false}, {"text": "90%", "added": false}, {"text": "85%", "added": false}, {"text": "75%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": "80%"}, {"n": 16, "text": "When difference between compound and simple interest for three years is ₹186 at 10% interest per annum, the principal is ₹______", "options": [{"text": "5425", "added": false}, {"text": "6420", "added": false}, {"text": "7200", "added": false}, {"text": "6000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "si-ci-difference", "key_answer": "6000"}, {"n": 17, "text": "A shopkeeper bought an article for ₹540. At what price (in ₹) should he sell the article to make 20% profit?", "options": [{"text": "648", "added": false}, {"text": "636", "added": false}, {"text": "432", "added": false}, {"text": "660", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": "648"}, {"n": 18, "text": "A medicine has 60% substance S and 40% substance T. If the cost price of S is increased from ₹30 to ₹40 per unit and the cost price of T is decreased to ₹20 from ₹30 per unit, then the cost of the medicine will _____ by _____%.", "options": [{"text": "decrease; 6.67", "added": false}, {"text": "decrease; 3.33", "added": false}, {"text": "increase; 3.33", "added": false}, {"text": "increase; 6.67", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": "increase; 6.67"}, {"n": 19, "text": "If 4% of x = 60, then x is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "3000", "added": false}, {"text": "1600", "added": false}, {"text": "1500", "added": false}, {"text": "3100", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": "1500"}, {"n": 20, "text": "A store offers two successive discounts of 12% and 18% on an item. What is the equivalent single discount that a customer would receive if these two discounts were applied together?", "options": [{"text": "26.46%", "added": false}, {"text": "27.84%", "added": false}, {"text": "30%", "added": false}, {"text": "28.64%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": "27.84%"}]}